.TH DAQ-STATUS.SH 1 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daq-status.sh \- report which DAQ partitions and environments are running
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daq-status.sh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIpartition\fR]
[\fB\-j\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-status.sh
cross-checks the operations configuration against the live tmux state
and prints one row per partition and active environment. It is
strictly read-only and safe to run against a partition that is taking
data.
.PP
Each environment is reported in one of four states:
.TP
.B RUNNING
The tmux window exists and \fBots\fR is the current command in one of
its panes.
.TP
.B STOPPED
The window exists but \fBots\fR is not running in it \(em typically a
crashed or manually exited instance.
.TP
.B NO-WINDOW
The session exists but this environment has no window, so it was never
started or its window was killed.
.TP
.B NO-SESSION
There is no tmux session for the partition at all.
.PP
A trailing summary lists the live \fBdaq\-*\fR tmux sessions with
their window counts and creation times.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then config file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Operations YAML to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Report only this partition. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_PARTITION\fR.
Default: every configured partition.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit JSON instead of the table, for scripted consumers.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print nothing. Exit 0 only if every active environment is
\fBRUNNING\fR, making the command usable as a health check.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAQ_STATUS_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was produced; with \fB\-q\fR, every active environment is
running.
.TP
.B 1
tmux is missing, the configuration could not be read, or, with
\fB\-q\fR, at least one environment is not running.
.TP
.B 2
A command line option was not recognised.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show every partition:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-status.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use it as a health check in a monitoring script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
if ! daq-status.sh -q -z partition_0; then
    echo "partition_0 is not fully up"
fi
.fi
.RE
.PP
Feed the state to another tool:
.PP
.RS
.nf
daq-status.sh --json | jq -r '.environments[] | select(.state != "RUNNING") | .environment'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
.BR stop-daq.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR tmux (1)
